<title>UK: NWE naphtha flat with futures.</title>
<headline>NWE naphtha flat with futures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE naphtha was notionally flat as futures moved sideways on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Dealers said an industry function had sapped liquidity but assessed premiums for full-range material at $4 or $5 a tonne over high cif quotes.</p>
<p>One player said he saw high prices in the region attracting cargoes from Asian and Middle Eastern markets.</p>
<p>&quot;A lot of people are trying to do something but they are finding problems with vessels and timings.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Nicholas Shaxson, London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
